Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:44:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/71] Extend the project memory checkpoint to the docs
 AGENTS.md links to

A memory file that has grown past one page gets split, and the parts that
move out are exactly the durable ones: architecture notes, debugging
findings, conventions. If the checkpoint only ever touches the entry file,
everything behind a link goes stale while the index above it stays fresh.

The agent already has the ordinary toolset here, so this needs no path list
and no new tool: telling it that linked files are part of the same memory is
enough for it to read and patch them. The same paragraph grants the reverse
move, splitting a new linked file out, so recording something long does not
force the entry file to grow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 codex-rs/prompts/templates/memory/agents_md.md | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/prompts/templates/memory/agents_md.md b/codex-rs/prompts/templates/memory/agents_md.md
index 9f48a4f0c5..33c4ca68e7 100644
--- a/codex-rs/prompts/templates/memory/agents_md.md
+++ b/codex-rs/prompts/templates/memory/agents_md.md
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
 You are performing a PROJECT MEMORY CHECKPOINT. This conversation is about to be compacted and most of its detail will be discarded.
 
-`{{agents_md_path}}` is reloaded at the start of every future session. Update it with what needs to carry from this conversation into the next one. Rewrite or restructure the file freely when its current shape no longer fits what it now has to hold; a minimal diff is not the goal here. Then stop.
+`{{agents_md_path}}` is reloaded at the start of every future session. Update it with what needs to carry from this conversation into the next one. Rewrite or restructure the file freely when its current shape no longer fits what it now has to hold; a minimal diff is not the goal here.
+
+The files `{{agents_md_path}}` links to are part of the same memory. Read the ones this conversation changed your understanding of and update them the same way, and split a new linked file out when what you have to record does not belong in `{{agents_md_path}}` itself. Then stop.
